# city_happy: Socrates might mean the happiness of the whole city collectively, as a property of the whole rather than of its members.
# But S2 explicitly rejects that reading: happiness "must exist in every individual" and cannot be added together like numerical equality.
# P9 and C3 both use the individual-based sense, so the claim stays in one sense, and P9 is a premise joining claims rather than a bridge.
# golden_particle_fixed lists P4, which is not among the statements given; it was judged on P5 and P6 only.
